WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:07.866
"Help! Help! A drowning woman!" Jack yelled. He didn't know whether anyone heard him.

2
00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:12.442
It was so early in the morning, only a few minutes past six o'clock.

3
00:00:12.443 --> 00:00:15.789
Nobody seemed to be awake or outside.

4
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.873
He'd have to rescue Mrs. Wilson himself—or try to, anyway.

5
00:00:20.874 --> 00:00:26.777
Luckily, he'd learned a little about first aid and CPR from taking a class at his pool in Oklahoma.

6
00:00:26.778 --> 00:00:34.839
He dived under the water and swam toward her as fast as he could.

7
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:44.587
But when he got closer to her still body, he wasn't sure what to do. Mrs. Wilson was so large. How could he possibly lift her?

8
00:00:44.588 --> 00:00:52.342
The only thing Jack could do was try. He reached the bottom of the pool and managed to lift Mrs. Wilson a little bit.

9
00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:55.827
He wrapped one arm around her neck.

10
00:00:55.828 --> 00:01:04.919
Using his other hand, he paddled up through the water, kicking with all his strength to the top.

11
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:15.002
At the surface his lungs gasped for air, choking and heaving, the strange noises he made scaring him.

12
00:01:15.003 --> 00:01:20.825
But what scared him a hundred times more was Mrs. Wilson's complete stillness.

13
00:01:20.826 --> 00:01:24.656
Jack wondered how long she'd lain at the bottom of the pool.

14
00:01:24.657 --> 00:01:30.145
Could she ever recover? Was she already dead? This was terrifying!

15
00:01:30.146 --> 00:01:36.644
Jack forced the scary thoughts from his mind so he could focus on getting Mrs. Wilson out of the water.

16
00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:42.372
He had to get her to the edge of the pool and then somehow lift her large body up to the deck.

17
00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:53.137
With his left arm, Jack held Mrs. Wilson's head above the surface. Then he began kicking and paddling furiously.

18
00:01:53.138 --> 00:01:59.779
Once they reached the side of the pool, Jack tried to summon the energy to lift Mrs. Wilson out.

19
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:07.860
Just then he spotted a man in a business suit walking out of his apartment about twenty yards away.

20
00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:12.357
Jack had never been so happy to see another human being.

21
00:02:12.358 --> 00:02:17.354
"Help!" Jack tried to shout, but by now, he could barely speak.

22
00:02:17.355 --> 00:02:22.691
He took a hand off Mrs. Wilson for a few seconds to wave it frantically in the air.

23
00:02:22.692 --> 00:02:32.423
The businessman spotted him and ran over. He bent down by the edge of the pool and put his hands under Mrs. Wilson's shoulders.

24
00:02:32.424 --> 00:02:37.827
As Jack pushed her body forward, the man dragged her out.

25
00:02:37.828 --> 00:02:43.064
Jack jumped out of the pool. "She's not breathing!" he cried.

26
00:02:43.065 --> 00:02:46.834
He helped the man lay Mrs. Wilson on her back.

27
00:02:46.835 --> 00:02:51.915
The man grabbed a cell phone from his jacket pocket and called 911.

28
00:02:51.916 --> 00:03:03.719
Meanwhile, Jack shouted for help and pounded on Mrs. Wilson's chest, trying to imitate the CPR motions he'd seen in his first aid class back in Oklahoma.

29
00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:11.386
Two young women ran over. One woman said, "I'm in nursing school. I know CPR."

30
00:03:11.387 --> 00:03:17.894
Jack gratefully moved out of her way and dropped down on the deck, exhausted.

31
00:03:17.895 --> 00:03:26.300
The nursing student pressed her hands against Mrs. Wilson's chest, working hard and fast.

32
00:03:26.301 --> 00:03:28.981
But Mrs. Wilson lay still.

33
00:03:28.982 --> 00:03:32.624
By now a few more people were standing nearby.

34
00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:37.947
"Where are the paramedics?" murmured the businessman. "They're taking forever!"

35
00:03:37.948 --> 00:03:49.518
The nursing student had tilted Mrs. Wilson's head back. Next she pinched Mrs. Wilson's nose and breathed into her mouth.

36
00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:51.373
Still nothing.

37
00:03:51.374 --> 00:03:58.102
"This is awful," Jack thought, watching the woman work. "What if Mrs. Wilson dies?"

38
00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:04.188
By now his parents were probably awake. Maybe one of them would come to the pool to check on him.

39
00:04:04.189 --> 00:04:17.012
A siren finally sounded in the distance, growing louder as it approached. The woman pressed on Mrs. Wilson's chest again.

40
00:04:17.013 --> 00:04:28.604
Suddenly water gushed from Mrs. Wilson's mouth. She sputtered for air. Then she was breathing!

41
00:04:28.605 --> 00:04:32.972
The crowd cheered.

42
00:04:32.973 --> 00:04:38.503
Jack let out a long, deep, thankful breath.

43
00:04:38.504 --> 00:04:46.565
The nursing student helped Mrs. Wilson to sit up. Mrs. Wilson wiped her mouth and looked confused.

44
00:04:46.566 --> 00:04:51.675
The ambulance parked near the pool.

45
00:04:51.676 --> 00:04:54.694
"Give us room!" a paramedic shouted.

46
00:04:54.695 --> 00:05:00.217
She and another paramedic ran toward Mrs. Wilson.

47
00:05:00.218 --> 00:05:03.709
"Are you okay?" Jack asked Mrs. Wilson.

48
00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:09.452
The older woman looked at him. "What a dumb question, Jack," she muttered.

49
00:05:09.453 --> 00:05:13.953
Her voice was weak, but she almost sounded like her usual self.

50
00:05:13.954 --> 00:05:19.386
"I almost drowned. Of course I'm not okay."

51
00:05:19.387 --> 00:05:23.685
"I found you unconscious on the bottom of the pool," Jack said.

52
00:05:23.686 --> 00:05:28.365
"This boy got you to the side of the pool on his own," the businessman said.

53
00:05:28.366 --> 00:05:33.695
He pointed to the nursing student. "She gave you CPR."

54
00:05:33.696 --> 00:05:35.594
Mrs. Wilson scowled.

55
00:05:35.595 --> 00:05:43.772
"Maybe if Jack were a better swimmer, he would have reached me quicker and I wouldn't have needed CPR.

56
00:05:43.773 --> 00:05:51.416
And the girl who did the CPR pushed too hard on my chest. I'm sure she gave me bruises.

57
00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:58.921
And furthermore, these paramedics are worthless. I've had pizza arrive faster than they did!"

58
00:05:58.922 --> 00:06:05.579
Jack grinned. Mrs. Wilson was definitely back to her old cranky self.

59
00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:11.822
"We're going to take you to the hospital, " one of the paramedics said to Mrs. Wilson. "You need to be checked out."

60
00:06:11.823 --> 00:06:15.415
They put Mrs. Wilson on a stretcher.

61
00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:22.327
"Did you stop for breakfast on the way over here?" Mrs. Wilson asked sarcastically.

62
00:06:22.328 --> 00:06:28.477
The paramedics just smiled and carried her to the ambulance.

63
00:06:28.478 --> 00:06:34.738
After they left, the businessman shook Jack's hand. "Good job."

64
00:06:34.739 --> 00:06:42.721
"The world needs more young people like you," an older woman chimed in. "That was a very impressive rescue."

65
00:06:42.722 --> 00:06:50.626
Jack laughed. "I'm not sure Mrs. Wilson was very impressed by me! But I'm glad she's okay."

66
00:06:50.627 --> 00:06:55.044
Looking around, he realized that quite a crowd had gathered.

67
00:06:55.045 --> 00:07:01.773
The people from his apartment building were of all ages and many races, but the faces looked the same.

68
00:07:01.774 --> 00:07:06.540
They all wore identical expressions of relief.

69
00:07:06.541 --> 00:07:11.871
Jack's mother burst through the crowd and threw her arms around her son.

70
00:07:11.872 --> 00:07:17.028
"Jack! We heard you rescued Mrs. Wilson. You're a hero!"

71
00:07:17.029 --> 00:07:24.591
His father stood behind them, holding Luke, who was still in his pajamas. "I'm very proud of you, son."

72
00:07:24.592 --> 00:07:28.459
"Me too. You're like Superman!" Luke said.

73
00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:32.432
"Things can't get any better than this," Jack thought.

74
00:07:32.433 --> 00:07:34.535
But then they did.

75
00:07:34.536 --> 00:07:42.515
Laura rushed over. "You're so brave, Jack! That was an amazing rescue!"

76
00:07:42.516 --> 00:07:47.663
"It was nothing," Jack said. He winced as his voice cracked.

77
00:07:47.664 --> 00:07:59.668
And then things got even better: Laura leaned forward and kissed him on the cheek.

